WEBVTT

1
00:03:07.521 --> 00:03:09.397
This is Batman. I've found them.

2
00:03:10.399 --> 00:03:13.609
Tell Cyborg he was right about how
they've been breaking into these places.

3
00:03:13.777 --> 00:03:15.111
Copy that.

4
00:03:15.278 --> 00:03:17.697
Hold your position. Help is on the wa...

5
00:03:28.917 --> 00:03:31.419
That's what I call a safecracker.

6
00:03:32.003 --> 00:03:33.879
How many times do I have to tell you?

7
00:03:34.047 --> 00:03:36.132
We don't want industrial diamonds.

8
00:03:36.299 --> 00:03:39.301
- But, boss...
- Listen to the King, Ten.

9
00:03:41.638 --> 00:03:43.764
Quality over quantity.

10
00:03:52.482 --> 00:03:54.525
Jack, we're on a timetable.

11
00:03:54.693 --> 00:03:56.152
What are you doing out there?

12
00:03:56.319 --> 00:03:58.320
Keeping watch.

13
00:04:11.084 --> 00:04:13.836
Peekaboo, I see you.

14
00:04:25.432 --> 00:04:27.600
Pick a card, any card.

15
00:04:48.997 --> 00:04:51.290
Cute. I can do this all day.

16
00:04:51.458 --> 00:04:52.958
Can you?

17
00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:56.128
Forget it, Jack.
Everybody, take what you can and get out.

18
00:04:56.296 --> 00:04:58.547
Right. Soon as I kill Batman.

19
00:05:06.473 --> 00:05:08.224
No way Batman came here alone.

20
00:05:10.602 --> 00:05:13.062
What, I'm supposed to be worried
about Robin?

21
00:05:21.947 --> 00:05:23.155
Huh?

22
00:05:26.618 --> 00:05:28.494
You might wanna give up now.

23
00:05:28.662 --> 00:05:30.704
Crap. It's the Justice League.

24
00:05:36.753 --> 00:05:38.087
That's three you owe me.

25
00:05:38.255 --> 00:05:40.381
- We keeping score?
- Not literally.

26
00:05:40.549 --> 00:05:43.592
Because if we are, it's 8 to 7, my favor.

27
00:05:56.439 --> 00:05:58.691
- Batman, are you okay?
- I'll live.

28
00:06:05.949 --> 00:06:07.700
So will Ace, apparently.

29
00:06:08.243 --> 00:06:10.452
He's still a little embarrassed
from last time.

30
00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:12.288
He sucker punched me.

31
00:06:16.084 --> 00:06:17.960
I've got Queen.

32
00:06:18.128 --> 00:06:21.130
That leaves Jack. Haven't seen him
since he sicced Ace on me.

33
00:06:21.298 --> 00:06:24.925
Couldn't have gone far. You search the vaults.
I'll take the rest of the building.

34
00:06:55.832 --> 00:06:57.166
Don't bother. I just looked.

35
00:06:57.334 --> 00:06:59.209
- Everywhere?
- The whole complex...

36
00:06:59.377 --> 00:07:01.587
except for the last vault room.
Shall we?

37
00:07:01.755 --> 00:07:05.007
- After you.
- Heh, like you've got a choice.

38
00:07:09.512 --> 00:07:11.347
- Found him.
- You fast enough to go in...

39
00:07:11.514 --> 00:07:13.933
and knock him out
before he glances in your direction?

40
00:07:14.309 --> 00:07:16.769
We could wait
until his eye laser runs out of power.

41
00:07:16.937 --> 00:07:19.939
Flank him. I'll make sure he stays inside
until you get there.

42
00:07:20.106 --> 00:07:22.149
That will work too.

43
00:07:26.488 --> 00:07:28.864
All right, now come the warning shots.

44
00:07:30.825 --> 00:07:32.534
Give up? Please say no.

45
00:07:32.702 --> 00:07:35.329
You'll never catch me, Lantern.

46
00:07:36.039 --> 00:07:37.998
Lots of women say that.

47
00:07:44.422 --> 00:07:45.965
Bang.

48
00:08:22.419 --> 00:08:23.752
Say good night, Ace.

49
00:08:42.772 --> 00:08:44.773
Surrender peacefully.
You will not be harmed.

50
00:08:44.941 --> 00:08:47.192
Really don't think so, martian.

51
00:09:04.461 --> 00:09:07.629
Come on in. I'll kill you where you stand.

52
00:09:09.466 --> 00:09:11.383
Trying to make me look away?

53
00:09:11.551 --> 00:09:12.801
It's not gonna work.

54
00:09:14.679 --> 00:09:16.138
I'm pretty sure it is, Jack.

55
00:09:19.601 --> 00:09:20.809
J'onn!

56
00:09:21.519 --> 00:09:24.396
I am unharmed.

57
00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:32.821
Intangibility. Works every time.

58
00:09:33.740 --> 00:09:35.657
- What?
- King escaped me.

59
00:09:35.825 --> 00:09:37.659
He was headed in that direction.

60
00:09:55.804 --> 00:09:58.305
Don't think so, Your Highness.

61
00:10:00.308 --> 00:10:03.685
Handheld plasma generator. Nice work.

62
00:10:03.853 --> 00:10:06.480
Hey, guys. You missed one,
but I got him for you.

63
00:10:08.316 --> 00:10:10.776
What were you doing here?
I thought you were helping.

64
00:10:10.944 --> 00:10:12.027
I am helping.

65
00:10:12.195 --> 00:10:16.198
Batman thought your robbery spree was
being done with extra-dimensional tech.

66
00:10:16.366 --> 00:10:17.616
You were right by the way.

67
00:10:17.784 --> 00:10:20.786
I asked him to consult
because his father did work in the field.

68
00:10:21.204 --> 00:10:23.539
Since Dad passed,
I'm the world's ranking expert...

69
00:10:23.706 --> 00:10:25.415
in multi-dimensional interface.

70
00:10:25.583 --> 00:10:29.044
The Royal Flush Gang knows more
about this tech than you?

71
00:10:29.212 --> 00:10:31.588
Somebody does, but not these mooks.

72
00:10:31.756 --> 00:10:34.466
Flying playing cards is one thing,
but this?

73
00:10:34.634 --> 00:10:39.054
Agreed, this isn't even their standard MO.
Anything on the hard drive?

74
00:10:39.222 --> 00:10:42.015
A lot. I'm still sorting it all out.

75
00:10:44.936 --> 00:10:46.395
Wake up, King.

76
00:10:46.896 --> 00:10:48.188
Got some questions for you.

77
00:10:49.566 --> 00:10:52.526
- I want a lawyer.
- You're getting ahead of yourself.

78
00:10:52.694 --> 00:10:55.320
First, you want a doctor,
then you want a lawyer.

79
00:10:55.864 --> 00:10:57.823
Diana, would you be so kind?

80
00:11:01.536 --> 00:11:04.204
You sure know how to take the fun
out of an interrogation.

81
00:11:04.372 --> 00:11:07.583
Who gave you the technology
that allows you to walk through walls?

82
00:11:08.042 --> 00:11:09.751
I do not know.

83
00:11:10.295 --> 00:11:12.713
The lasso compels you to tell the truth.

84
00:11:12.881 --> 00:11:14.673
I do not know.

85
00:11:16.050 --> 00:11:20.387
- I know you don't like to do it, J'onn....
- Not unnecessarily.

86
00:11:28.521 --> 00:11:30.898
I've read the minds of his entire group.

87
00:11:31.065 --> 00:11:33.442
None of them knows the origin
of the device.

88
00:11:33.610 --> 00:11:35.611
Then we haven't found
the end of the thread.

89
00:11:35.778 --> 00:11:37.613
We've found all we're going to tonight.

90
00:11:37.780 --> 00:11:41.533
I'll take these guys to booking. The rest
of you can sleep on what we've learned.

91
00:11:41.701 --> 00:11:45.204
- I don't need to sleep, I need to follow up...
- Your injuries are severe.

92
00:11:45.371 --> 00:11:49.374
If you wish, a session with my healing ray
could save you days of recovery time.

93
00:11:49.542 --> 00:11:50.918
I'm fine, Diana.

94
00:11:51.085 --> 00:11:52.377
Well, I'm tired.

95
00:11:52.545 --> 00:11:56.256
Unless something comes up, we'll
reconvene at the meeting on Thursday.

96
00:11:56.424 --> 00:11:59.134
I think we could search the hard drive
on the device for...

97
00:11:59.302 --> 00:12:01.470
I've got 16 petabytes of data
to sort through.

98
00:12:01.638 --> 00:12:05.224
I'll call you as soon
as I've got something. Honest.

99
00:12:15.235 --> 00:12:17.736
Authorized vehicle operator recognized.

100
00:12:17.904 --> 00:12:20.489
Security systems disarmed.

101
00:12:51.521 --> 00:12:53.730
Late night playing cards, Master Bruce?

102
00:12:53.898 --> 00:12:56.692
Something like that. How did you know?

103
00:12:58.027 --> 00:13:01.530
I believe tradition calls
for hiding these up one's sleeves.

104
00:13:01.698 --> 00:13:03.198
Was that sarcasm, Alfred?

105
00:13:03.366 --> 00:13:04.700
Mild teasing, at best.

106
00:13:04.867 --> 00:13:07.286
I'm being uncharacteristically gentle
with you...

107
00:13:07.453 --> 00:13:11.206
mainly because you're bleeding
all over my nice clean floor.

108
00:13:13.543 --> 00:13:15.669
Not going to let me go to work.

109
00:13:15.837 --> 00:13:17.587
That is correct, Master Bruce.

110
00:13:17.755 --> 00:13:20.257
- Not until you've had medical attention...
- Fine.

111
00:13:20.425 --> 00:13:23.302
Food, and a minimum
of eight hours bed rest.

112
00:13:23.469 --> 00:13:24.886
Let's just get this over with.

113
00:13:25.054 --> 00:13:27.431
I made chicken soup.
You can eat while you brood...

114
00:13:27.598 --> 00:13:31.393
and I'll put in your stitches myself.
It will be delightful, I'm sure.

115
00:13:31.561 --> 00:13:32.602
All right.

116
00:13:32.770 --> 00:13:38.108
By the way, the part about
the stitches? That would be sarcasm.

117
00:13:45.992 --> 00:13:47.701
This is Mirror Master. I'm in.

118
00:13:47.869 --> 00:13:49.244
Then get to work.

119
00:13:49.412 --> 00:13:51.580
This is the most vulnerable moment
of the entire plan.

120
00:14:00.340 --> 00:14:02.007
You sure this thing will work?

121
00:14:02.175 --> 00:14:06.011
For the amount of money
I paid LexCorp, it had better.

122
00:14:08.348 --> 00:14:10.807
I couldn't see anything
while I was in the mirror.

123
00:14:10.975 --> 00:14:14.394
Maybe I should snoop around
and see if I can find out who he really is.

124
00:14:14.562 --> 00:14:17.356
The information I sent you to steal
is far more valuable...

125
00:14:17.523 --> 00:14:19.316
than Batman's secret identity.

126
00:14:19.484 --> 00:14:22.110
Besides, I already know it.

127
00:14:22.278 --> 00:14:24.613
- You know who Batma...?
- Download complete.

128
00:15:14.163 --> 00:15:16.123
It's not broken.

129
00:15:19.001 --> 00:15:20.544
You've arrived.

130
00:15:20.711 --> 00:15:22.462
Star Sapphire.

131
00:15:22.630 --> 00:15:27.300
If this is an elaborate ambush, you won't
fare any better than the alligator.

132
00:15:27.468 --> 00:15:29.719
I suspect we'd do a bit better.

133
00:15:29.887 --> 00:15:31.263
It's Bane, isn't it?

134
00:15:31.431 --> 00:15:33.932
I'm Metallo. Big fan of your work.

135
00:15:38.354 --> 00:15:40.856
The scary guy's Ma'alefa'ak...

136
00:15:41.023 --> 00:15:44.443
and the lady with the claws
is Cheetah.

137
00:16:14.974 --> 00:16:19.102
- What's that supposed to be?
- An invitation.

138
00:16:37.038 --> 00:16:38.997
Welcome to the Hall of Doom.

139
00:16:39.415 --> 00:16:40.999
I'm Vandal Savage.

140
00:16:41.167 --> 00:16:42.876
I'm pleased to see you all here.

141
00:16:43.044 --> 00:16:46.588
For $10 million,
I'm inclined to accept any invitation.

142
00:16:46.756 --> 00:16:47.923
Makes me wonder, though.

143
00:16:48.090 --> 00:16:50.884
What if we'd just kept the money
and not shown up?

144
00:16:51.052 --> 00:16:53.428
You'd live the rest
of your very short lives...

145
00:16:53.596 --> 00:16:56.431
in fear of the moment
when I would inevitably find you.

146
00:16:56.599 --> 00:16:57.682
Tough talk.

147
00:16:57.850 --> 00:16:59.434
None of us are that easy to kill.

148
00:16:59.602 --> 00:17:02.020
Everybody dies, child.

149
00:17:02.188 --> 00:17:04.105
That's not what I've heard about you.

150
00:17:05.358 --> 00:17:08.527
You five and Mirror Master are here
because you each have...

151
00:17:08.694 --> 00:17:11.696
a personal vendetta
against a member of the Justice League.

152
00:17:11.864 --> 00:17:13.323
You wish to see them dead.

153
00:17:13.491 --> 00:17:15.825
While I have no personal enmity
towards them...

154
00:17:15.993 --> 00:17:19.371
I have a vision for this world,
and they would stand in my way.

155
00:17:19.789 --> 00:17:22.958
Their deaths would serve my goals.

156
00:17:24.085 --> 00:17:27.128
In short, we need each other.

157
00:17:27.296 --> 00:17:30.006
I don't speak for the others,
but I'm perfectly capable...

158
00:17:30.174 --> 00:17:32.175
of killing Wonder Woman by myself.

159
00:17:32.343 --> 00:17:34.928
History says otherwise.

160
00:17:35.096 --> 00:17:39.307
You've all tried and failed to kill members
of the league on multiple occasions.

161
00:17:39.475 --> 00:17:42.310
Savage has foolproof plans
for how we can destroy them.

162
00:17:42.478 --> 00:17:45.647
And I will pay you $100 million,
plus expenses...

163
00:17:45.815 --> 00:17:48.149
for each Justice Leaguer
you take off the table.

164
00:17:48.317 --> 00:17:51.444
Wait a minute. You just committed
over a half a billion dollars...

165
00:17:51.612 --> 00:17:54.990
just to get the JLA out of the way
of another plan?

166
00:17:55.157 --> 00:17:58.660
As Ma'alefa'ak implied earlier,
I'm very old.

167
00:17:58.828 --> 00:18:01.871
Fifty thousand years has been
sufficient time to amass a fortune...

168
00:18:02.039 --> 00:18:04.124
that dwarfs any other
in human history.

169
00:18:04.292 --> 00:18:07.877
Even so, to spend that much money
just to clear the decks...

170
00:18:08.045 --> 00:18:09.754
the payoff must be huge.

171
00:18:09.922 --> 00:18:11.464
Inconceivably so.

172
00:18:11.632 --> 00:18:15.510
Any who would like to continue working
with me are welcome to share in the riches.

173
00:18:15.678 --> 00:18:18.179
After you've destroyed
the Justice League.

174
00:18:19.515 --> 00:18:22.100
I don't see any of us looking for the exit.

175
00:18:22.685 --> 00:18:23.852
Then it's settled.

176
00:18:24.604 --> 00:18:27.856
Welcome to the Legion of Doom.

177
00:18:35.865 --> 00:18:37.741
Master Bruce.

178
00:18:38.659 --> 00:18:39.868
What is it, Alfred?

179
00:18:40.911 --> 00:18:44.539
I have some unpleasant news.

180
00:18:47.877 --> 00:18:49.377
No.

181
00:18:51.881 --> 00:18:53.423
How could this have happened?

182
00:18:53.591 --> 00:18:56.551
Where are my parents' caskets?

183
00:18:56.969 --> 00:18:58.219
I don't know, sir.

184
00:18:58.387 --> 00:19:00.722
We found it like this
just a few minutes ago.

185
00:19:00.890 --> 00:19:02.724
I called the house right away.

186
00:19:02.892 --> 00:19:05.310
Whoever did this is going to pay.

187
00:19:05.478 --> 00:19:07.646
Perhaps I can help you with that.

188
00:19:09.398 --> 00:19:12.359
When I said I didn't know
who was responsible for this...

189
00:19:13.736 --> 00:19:15.320
I may have been lying.

190
00:19:15.488 --> 00:19:16.821
What?

191
00:19:33.589 --> 00:19:35.006
Come on, John.

192
00:19:35.174 --> 00:19:36.549
We actually surprised you?

193
00:19:36.717 --> 00:19:39.928
It's been a busy week.
I'd forgotten it was my birthday.

194
00:19:40.096 --> 00:19:42.097
Also, I'd never mentioned it
to any of you.

195
00:19:42.264 --> 00:19:44.349
Your stalker knows all.

196
00:19:45.226 --> 00:19:46.768
She really likes you, you know.

197
00:19:54.527 --> 00:19:57.779
I didn't know how old you were,
so I just put a lot.

198
00:20:01.742 --> 00:20:04.202
You're supposed to wait for us
to sing "Happy Birthday."

199
00:20:04.370 --> 00:20:07.789
Ugh, I hope you at least made a wish.

200
00:20:10.126 --> 00:20:11.292
I didn't order that.

201
00:20:11.460 --> 00:20:13.128
It's from the lady.

202
00:20:15.756 --> 00:20:17.298
Do you know her?

203
00:20:17.466 --> 00:20:19.300
I do not.

204
00:20:22.054 --> 00:20:24.639
Thank you for the drink, but I'm on duty.

205
00:20:24.807 --> 00:20:26.975
I figured. It's a soda.

206
00:20:31.230 --> 00:20:33.481
- Got a light?
- I don't smoke.

207
00:20:35.693 --> 00:20:37.610
You seem very familiar.

208
00:20:37.778 --> 00:20:39.237
You don't need a line, John.

209
00:20:39.405 --> 00:20:41.614
I'm obviously interested in you.

210
00:20:41.782 --> 00:20:43.450
I can't place your face.

211
00:20:43.617 --> 00:20:45.285
That's unusual for me.

212
00:20:45.661 --> 00:20:47.203
Really look.

213
00:20:47.371 --> 00:20:49.122
Use your martian vision.

214
00:20:49.290 --> 00:20:51.040
How do you...?

215
00:21:02.094 --> 00:21:03.762
What do you want, Cheetah?

216
00:21:03.929 --> 00:21:06.347
To hurt you, Diana. What else?

217
00:21:24.784 --> 00:21:25.992
Hey, can we wrap this up?

218
00:21:26.160 --> 00:21:29.120
We're blocking traffic,
and it's obvious what happened here.

219
00:21:29.413 --> 00:21:30.455
Is it?

220
00:21:30.623 --> 00:21:33.708
Come on, Allen,
don't do this to me again.

221
00:21:33.876 --> 00:21:36.878
- The facts don't fit the scenario.
- You guys hear the news?

222
00:21:37.046 --> 00:21:40.423
You mean the part where I blow
my date tonight and therefore die alone...

223
00:21:40.591 --> 00:21:43.134
because Allen turned my hit-and-run
into a homicide?

224
00:21:43.302 --> 00:21:47.555
I'm serious. Mirror Master's robbing
the new maglev train from Keystone City.

225
00:21:47.723 --> 00:21:52.560
Bag and tag everything, and be thorough.
This is a murder, not an accident.

226
00:21:52.937 --> 00:21:54.896
- Where you going?
- Train station.

227
00:21:55.064 --> 00:21:58.149
For what? It's a robbery in progress,
not a crime scene.

228
00:21:58.317 --> 00:22:01.903
Mirror Master's there.
It'll be a crime scene soon enough.

229
00:22:20.881 --> 00:22:22.382
Who's the officer in charge?

230
00:22:22.550 --> 00:22:24.926
Special Agent Porter.
My office reached out to you.

231
00:22:25.094 --> 00:22:28.513
An unknown number of heavily armed
militiamen have taken over the mine.

232
00:22:28.681 --> 00:22:31.558
A salt mine? For what?

233
00:22:31.725 --> 00:22:34.185
They call themselves
the Identity Brotherhood.

234
00:22:34.353 --> 00:22:38.356
They plan to use the salt mine as their base
during the second American revolution...

235
00:22:38.524 --> 00:22:40.400
which is, they claim, imminent.

236
00:22:40.568 --> 00:22:43.111
They've killed a dozen people,
wounded three of my men.

237
00:22:43.279 --> 00:22:45.697
- Why not go in hard and take them down?
- I'd like to.

238
00:22:45.865 --> 00:22:49.325
But they have at least six hostages,
workers, trapped down there with them.

239
00:22:49.493 --> 00:22:52.287
We hoped you might be able
to take a more subtle approach...

240
00:22:52.454 --> 00:22:54.414
than the responses we have available.

241
00:22:54.582 --> 00:22:55.790
Got it.

242
00:22:56.625 --> 00:22:59.711
This is Green Lantern. I'm coming in.

243
00:22:59.879 --> 00:23:03.965
If you harm any of those hostages,
you'll answer to me.

244
00:23:04.133 --> 00:23:05.258
Back in five.

245
00:23:42.504 --> 00:23:44.339
- Flash.
- Mirror Master's in here.

246
00:23:44.506 --> 00:23:47.759
- One at a time.
- We're shipping old cash to the reserve.

247
00:23:47.927 --> 00:23:50.553
- Old cash?
- It's being taken out of circulation.

248
00:23:50.721 --> 00:23:52.847
It'll be destroyed
and replaced with new bills.

249
00:23:53.015 --> 00:23:56.768
Unless Mirror Master steals it first,
which ain't gonna happen on my watch.

250
00:23:56.936 --> 00:24:01.105
Yeah. I just untied you, remember?
You're lucky he let you live.

251
00:24:01.273 --> 00:24:03.858
Stay here and I'll take a crack at him.

252
00:24:11.700 --> 00:24:13.868
Took you long enough to get here.

253
00:24:14.036 --> 00:24:15.870
I brought you something.

254
00:24:17.831 --> 00:24:19.207
I thought this was a robbery.

255
00:24:19.375 --> 00:24:22.293
It looks more like you're doing
the feds' work for them.

256
00:24:25.839 --> 00:24:28.883
Hologram. Figures.

257
00:24:30.761 --> 00:24:32.804
Which one of us is real?

258
00:24:32.972 --> 00:24:34.555
I don't care.

259
00:25:00.457 --> 00:25:04.836
What did you do with their bodies?

260
00:25:05.004 --> 00:25:08.923
When we fought before, I broke the bat.

261
00:25:09.091 --> 00:25:12.844
Today, I break the man.

262
00:25:20.978 --> 00:25:23.438
Come on, I'm not gonna kill you yet.

263
00:25:23.856 --> 00:25:25.106
What's in the box?

264
00:25:25.274 --> 00:25:26.524
Dead grandma.

265
00:25:26.692 --> 00:25:28.484
- What kind of sick...?
- Relax.

266
00:25:28.652 --> 00:25:30.278
I got a little ahead of myself.

267
00:25:30.446 --> 00:25:34.240
You can hardly blame me
trying to keep up with the likes of you.

268
00:25:36.201 --> 00:25:38.119
She's still alive.

269
00:25:41.790 --> 00:25:43.750
Don't move.

270
00:25:43.917 --> 00:25:46.210
You really wanna hear all this first.

271
00:25:46.378 --> 00:25:49.464
I call this my hostage box.

272
00:25:49.631 --> 00:25:52.341
At the end of the countdown,
already in progress...

273
00:25:52.509 --> 00:25:55.803
the box will activate
and instantly kill the old woman...

274
00:25:55.971 --> 00:25:58.973
unless you use your super-speed
to get her out.

275
00:25:59.391 --> 00:26:01.434
- It's a trap.
- Most probably...

276
00:26:01.602 --> 00:26:05.271
but you can't take that chance,
or pass up the challenge.

277
00:26:05.647 --> 00:26:08.316
Are you fast enough, Flash?

278
00:26:13.655 --> 00:26:16.407
Careful. It's bolted through your wrist.

279
00:26:16.825 --> 00:26:20.661
- What?
- It's a bomb with a three-mile blast radius.

280
00:26:20.829 --> 00:26:22.914
If you try to remove the bomb,
it explodes.

281
00:26:23.082 --> 00:26:26.042
If you do nothing in 60 seconds,
it explodes.

282
00:26:26.210 --> 00:26:29.337
Before you heroically leave the train
to protect the passengers...

283
00:26:29.505 --> 00:26:30.963
there's one last thing.

284
00:26:31.131 --> 00:26:34.008
Once you start running,
if you decelerate...

285
00:26:34.176 --> 00:26:35.343
It explodes.

286
00:26:35.511 --> 00:26:37.970
You've got 12 seconds
to decide what to do.

287
00:26:38.138 --> 00:26:42.600
I don't much care which way you go
because I'm not really here.

288
00:26:51.693 --> 00:26:54.028
Why are you here, Ma'alefa'ak?

289
00:26:54.196 --> 00:26:55.696
To buy you a drink.

290
00:26:55.864 --> 00:27:00.284
It's laced with a chemical
that has an odd effect on martian biology.

291
00:27:00.452 --> 00:27:03.037
You couldn't taste it over the soda.

292
00:27:06.041 --> 00:27:07.708
It's a poison.

293
00:27:07.876 --> 00:27:13.214
Oh, it won't kill you. Your body
will filter it out in a few hours.

294
00:27:14.049 --> 00:27:19.137
Unfortunately, you'll sweat the poison
out of your pores.

295
00:27:19.304 --> 00:27:21.556
It's magnesium, by the way.

296
00:27:21.723 --> 00:27:22.849
No.

297
00:27:26.353 --> 00:27:29.230
- John.
- That guy just fell down.

298
00:27:29.398 --> 00:27:31.399
What's the matter,
can't hold your liquor?

299
00:27:31.567 --> 00:27:34.026
- Stay back.
- Oh, man.

300
00:27:34.194 --> 00:27:36.070
He's the freaking Martian Manhunter.

301
00:27:39.741 --> 00:27:42.618
Listen, you must get everyone
away from me.

302
00:27:42.786 --> 00:27:44.912
You're all in grave danger.

303
00:27:52.713 --> 00:27:54.881
- Let's get out of here.
- Let's get out of here.

304
00:27:56.425 --> 00:27:57.550
Hold on, John.

305
00:28:05.601 --> 00:28:07.185
Stop, drop and roll, partner.

306
00:28:07.352 --> 00:28:09.228
Hang in there, we'll get this...

307
00:28:16.361 --> 00:28:18.446
He doesn't smoke.

308
00:28:20.282 --> 00:28:22.241
I think that guy's gonna jump.

309
00:28:22.409 --> 00:28:24.368
- Does anybody know him?
- I don't know.

310
00:28:24.536 --> 00:28:26.454
- Can you see him?
- Working on it, Lois.

311
00:28:28.290 --> 00:28:30.082
I think that guy works for our paper.

312
00:28:37.549 --> 00:28:40.384
The bond issue should easily cover
the budget shortfall...

313
00:28:40.552 --> 00:28:43.054
into the third quarter
of our next fiscal year.

314
00:28:44.431 --> 00:28:46.511
We all know the federal money
was a one-time thing...

315
00:28:46.642 --> 00:28:49.143
- ...to help boost the economy.
- Hello?

316
00:28:49.311 --> 00:28:51.437
It's me.
You know Henry Ackerdson?

317
00:28:51.855 --> 00:28:54.440
Used to be White House beat,
got downsized.

318
00:28:54.608 --> 00:28:57.902
- He was a good reporter. A real shame.
- It's about to be a bigger shame.

319
00:28:58.070 --> 00:29:00.279
He's going to jump off of the top
of the Daily Planet.

320
00:29:00.572 --> 00:29:02.406
I'm on my way.

321
00:29:12.876 --> 00:29:14.460
That's far enough, Lantern.

322
00:29:14.878 --> 00:29:19.173
You make a move, any move, and that drill's
coming down on their heads.

323
00:29:19.341 --> 00:29:23.344
You're not in a position to make a deal.
Step away from the control panel...

324
00:29:23.512 --> 00:29:26.347
and you won't get hurt.
There's no other way out of this.

325
00:29:35.440 --> 00:29:38.651
The shut-off is controlled
from one of the other consoles.

326
00:29:38.819 --> 00:29:40.820
I'll tell you which one if you let me go.

327
00:30:02.384 --> 00:30:07.888
That bracelet trick always impresses me,
but at least I got you once.

328
00:30:15.439 --> 00:30:17.732
You drugged me.

329
00:30:18.567 --> 00:30:20.651
Catch me if you can.

330
00:30:26.742 --> 00:30:29.243
It's not possible.

331
00:30:29.578 --> 00:30:32.163
- Wonder Woman.
- Look, it's Wonder Woman.

332
00:30:32.331 --> 00:30:33.664
- It's Wonder Woman.
- No way.

333
00:30:33.832 --> 00:30:35.708
- Wonder Woman.
- What's she doing here?

334
00:30:35.876 --> 00:30:38.085
- Wonder Woman.
- Dude, she's so hot.

335
00:30:38.253 --> 00:30:41.005
- Is it really her?
- Is that Wonder Woman?

336
00:30:41.173 --> 00:30:43.758
Why is she looking at us like that?

337
00:30:47.346 --> 00:30:50.598
- Hey, is that...?
- There he is!

338
00:30:53.435 --> 00:30:55.144
Mr. Ackerdson?

339
00:30:55.312 --> 00:30:56.520
May I call you Henry?

340
00:30:56.688 --> 00:30:58.314
Call me whatever you want.

341
00:30:58.482 --> 00:31:00.191
It doesn't matter.

342
00:31:00.359 --> 00:31:01.859
Nothing does.

343
00:31:02.027 --> 00:31:04.612
I'm going to have
to disagree with you, sir.

344
00:31:04.780 --> 00:31:06.364
Everything matters.

345
00:31:06.531 --> 00:31:07.865
Everybody matters.

346
00:31:08.033 --> 00:31:10.409
Don't come any closer. I'll do it.

347
00:31:11.453 --> 00:31:13.537
I'm staying right here.

348
00:31:19.961 --> 00:31:22.380
I want you to get out of here
as quickly as you can.

349
00:31:22.547 --> 00:31:25.132
Follow the light,
it's a safe path back to the surface.

350
00:31:25.300 --> 00:31:27.426
- They've still got Carol.
- Carol?

351
00:31:27.594 --> 00:31:30.137
From Bookkeeping.
They took her hostage first.

352
00:31:30.972 --> 00:31:32.640
I'll get her out. Go.

353
00:32:06.842 --> 00:32:08.300
Help me.

354
00:32:09.302 --> 00:32:10.886
Don't hurt her.

355
00:32:11.054 --> 00:32:12.388
It'll do you no good.

356
00:32:12.556 --> 00:32:14.807
All your partners are captured, or worse.

357
00:32:14.975 --> 00:32:17.101
- All of them?
- All of them.

358
00:32:17.269 --> 00:32:19.186
You've got no options.

359
00:32:20.313 --> 00:32:22.273
I've got one.

360
00:32:41.084 --> 00:32:42.209
No.

361
00:32:49.050 --> 00:32:50.551
I don't understand.

362
00:32:50.719 --> 00:32:52.344
Why didn't I disarm him?

363
00:32:52.512 --> 00:32:54.180
Why didn't I...?

364
00:32:56.475 --> 00:32:57.641
Oh, no.

365
00:33:04.024 --> 00:33:05.941
I'm so sorry.

366
00:33:07.194 --> 00:33:09.820
She sort of looks like me, doesn't she?

367
00:33:12.741 --> 00:33:13.741
Carol?

368
00:33:13.909 --> 00:33:17.286
Yes. Her name was Carol too.

369
00:33:17.454 --> 00:33:21.207
She's beautiful, of course,
and she has dark hair like mine.

370
00:33:21.374 --> 00:33:24.585
And the stench of your failure
hanging over her.

371
00:33:25.170 --> 00:33:26.212
I didn't mean...

372
00:33:26.379 --> 00:33:28.923
You didn't mean
to get all those people killed?

373
00:33:29.090 --> 00:33:34.011
You didn't mean to betray me,
drive me into becoming this?

374
00:33:34.596 --> 00:33:37.264
What didn't you mean, Hal?

375
00:33:37.432 --> 00:33:39.183
I don't know. I'm...

376
00:33:39.351 --> 00:33:40.559
Afraid?

377
00:33:40.727 --> 00:33:43.854
Afraid that you don't deserve
to have so much power?

378
00:33:44.022 --> 00:33:46.524
That nobody does?

379
00:33:47.442 --> 00:33:48.609
Yes.

380
00:33:49.444 --> 00:33:51.320
I don't deserve this.

381
00:33:51.488 --> 00:33:54.698
Then I hope you have the decency
to do what's right...

382
00:33:54.866 --> 00:33:58.118
and suffer for your many sins.

383
00:34:20.725 --> 00:34:22.518
You don't understand.

384
00:34:22.686 --> 00:34:25.020
I've been a newspaperman for 40 years.

385
00:34:25.188 --> 00:34:28.190
I started as a copyboy when I was 16.

386
00:34:28.358 --> 00:34:32.152
Always thought I'd be doing it
until the day I died.

387
00:34:32.320 --> 00:34:34.780
Heh, guess I got that part right.

388
00:34:34.948 --> 00:34:36.907
There are other jobs.

389
00:34:37.075 --> 00:34:39.201
Newspapers are dying.

390
00:34:39.369 --> 00:34:44.081
I spent my life fighting for the little
guy, fighting for truth and justice.

391
00:34:44.249 --> 00:34:46.041
It isn't relevant anymore.

392
00:34:46.209 --> 00:34:48.002
That's what some people say.

393
00:34:48.169 --> 00:34:51.797
But I've fought for the same things,
even when they don't seem fashionable.

394
00:34:51.965 --> 00:34:55.884
It's a never-ending battle,
but we can't quit.

395
00:34:57.304 --> 00:35:00.180
I'm not the man you think I am.

396
00:35:00.348 --> 00:35:02.683
I'm too weak to fight anymore.

397
00:35:02.851 --> 00:35:05.477
You're stronger than you know,
Mr. Ackerdson.

398
00:35:23.705 --> 00:35:25.456
Kryptonite bullet.

399
00:35:30.045 --> 00:35:31.837
Kryptonite heart.

400
00:36:20.095 --> 00:36:21.679
No!

401
00:36:31.940 --> 00:36:33.273
Hello, Bruce.

402
00:36:33.441 --> 00:36:35.651
Sorry I couldn't be there for this...

403
00:36:35.819 --> 00:36:38.654
but I have a rather large check
to pick up.

404
00:36:38.822 --> 00:36:41.407
Payment for dealing with you.

405
00:36:41.574 --> 00:36:46.078
Oh, you were concerned
about where I put your parents.

406
00:36:46.246 --> 00:36:47.371
Don't be.

407
00:36:47.539 --> 00:36:49.581
They're very close.

408
00:36:53.044 --> 00:36:54.795
Rest in peace.

409
00:37:19.946 --> 00:37:22.489
It was easier than I thought.

410
00:37:23.158 --> 00:37:24.241
To victory.

411
00:37:24.409 --> 00:37:25.659
To victory.

412
00:37:25.827 --> 00:37:27.578
To the Legion of Doom.

413
00:37:27.746 --> 00:37:29.663
To the Legion of Doom.

414
00:37:29.831 --> 00:37:32.332
Wait. A further toast.

415
00:37:32.500 --> 00:37:35.836
I've been trying to kill Batman
for nearly 10 years.

416
00:37:36.004 --> 00:37:39.882
Well, this time,
I did better than kill him...

417
00:37:40.049 --> 00:37:42.176
I humiliated him.

418
00:37:42.343 --> 00:37:43.802
Hear, hear.

419
00:37:43.970 --> 00:37:46.722
Each of us finally got the better
of our opposite numbers...

420
00:37:46.890 --> 00:37:50.017
and it's all thanks
to the genius of one man...

421
00:37:50.185 --> 00:37:51.852
Vandal Savage.

422
00:37:52.020 --> 00:37:54.062
- Yes, he's the man.
- Ha, ha, to the man.

423
00:37:54.230 --> 00:37:56.690
- And his checks clear.
- I love my money.

424
00:38:02.363 --> 00:38:04.490
Our business is completed.

425
00:38:04.657 --> 00:38:06.658
You are, of course, free to go.

426
00:38:07.035 --> 00:38:10.621
You hinted at a larger scheme and said
there would be a place for us in it...

427
00:38:10.789 --> 00:38:11.955
should we so choose.

428
00:38:12.582 --> 00:38:13.707
I did.

429
00:38:13.875 --> 00:38:16.293
And the offer remains open to you all.

430
00:38:16.461 --> 00:38:19.630
But I fear you may lack the vision
to go along with me.

431
00:38:20.089 --> 00:38:23.050
The next stage of my plans
might be considered...

432
00:38:23.218 --> 00:38:24.802
genocidal.

433
00:38:25.386 --> 00:38:27.805
What are you gonna do,
destroy the world?

434
00:38:27.972 --> 00:38:29.723
Nothing so crude.

435
00:38:29.891 --> 00:38:32.684
Half. Two-thirds at the most.

436
00:38:36.689 --> 00:38:38.232
It's not a joke.

437
00:38:38.399 --> 00:38:41.485
It's the next step in a plan
to transform the planet in a manner...

438
00:38:41.653 --> 00:38:47.366
that will render your $100-million
payday both trivial and meaningless.

439
00:38:47.534 --> 00:38:51.328
What possible profit could there be
in destroying the world?

440
00:38:51.496 --> 00:38:54.832
The first thing you have to understand
is that I am old.

441
00:38:54.999 --> 00:38:56.583
Older than the human race.

442
00:38:56.751 --> 00:38:59.378
I know that you believe this to be true.

443
00:38:59.921 --> 00:39:02.130
It is true.

444
00:39:02.841 --> 00:39:04.883
Eighty thousand years ago...

445
00:39:05.051 --> 00:39:08.595
I was living in
what is now the island of Sumatra.

446
00:39:09.556 --> 00:39:13.058
One night,
the sky lit up with streaks of fire.

447
00:39:13.434 --> 00:39:15.143
Meteors.

448
00:39:15.311 --> 00:39:19.565
But my primitive mind thought the stars
were falling from the sky.

449
00:39:24.946 --> 00:39:27.531
One meteor fell to Earth in my valley.

450
00:39:27.699 --> 00:39:29.658
My compatriots ran...

451
00:39:29.826 --> 00:39:34.621
but it was very cold
and the glowing stone was warm.

452
00:39:39.085 --> 00:39:40.627
I slept there...

453
00:39:40.795 --> 00:39:44.089
bathed in the meteor's
strange radiations.

454
00:39:44.257 --> 00:39:49.136
And when I awoke the next morning,
I was forever changed.

455
00:39:51.347 --> 00:39:54.850
The radiation mutated me, evolving me.

456
00:39:55.018 --> 00:39:58.687
I was instantly aware
of my increased intelligence.

457
00:40:00.607 --> 00:40:05.485
It was only with the passage of time
that I discovered the rest of my gift.

458
00:40:05.653 --> 00:40:09.656
So far as I know, I cannot die.

459
00:40:09.824 --> 00:40:11.325
Is that a fact?

460
00:40:12.076 --> 00:40:13.327
Go ahead.

461
00:40:24.797 --> 00:40:27.466
- Why'd you do that?
- Don't you realize what he's planning?

462
00:40:27.634 --> 00:40:30.677
In his new world,
our money doesn't matter.

463
00:40:33.348 --> 00:40:34.765
You are correct.

464
00:40:34.933 --> 00:40:36.350
Money won't matter.

465
00:40:36.517 --> 00:40:38.352
It's trivial in the long run.

466
00:40:41.022 --> 00:40:43.315
Let me tell you about the long run.

467
00:40:43.483 --> 00:40:44.858
I've lived thousands of lives.

468
00:40:45.026 --> 00:40:49.947
I've been a laborer, a scientist, a priest,
an artist, a healer, a thief.

469
00:40:50.114 --> 00:40:52.950
But most often a conqueror.

470
00:40:55.954 --> 00:40:58.538
I'm still not seeing
how this makes up for my money.

471
00:40:59.040 --> 00:41:02.125
Seventy-five thousand years ago...

472
00:41:02.293 --> 00:41:04.962
a disaster
nearly rendered humanity extinct.

473
00:41:05.129 --> 00:41:09.174
I enslaved the survivors
and ruled with an iron hand.

474
00:41:09.342 --> 00:41:10.676
In a few generations...

475
00:41:10.843 --> 00:41:13.762
my people were well under way
to repopulating the Earth...

476
00:41:13.930 --> 00:41:17.557
and becoming the planet's
dominant species.

477
00:41:17.725 --> 00:41:20.060
I was happy then.

478
00:41:20.228 --> 00:41:22.896
You're taking the world over
out of nostalgia?

479
00:41:23.064 --> 00:41:26.817
I'm taking over because humanity
is prideful and belligerent...

480
00:41:26.985 --> 00:41:29.528
and once again
needs my guiding hand.

481
00:41:29.696 --> 00:41:33.073
But before I take over,
I intend to soften them up.

482
00:41:33.241 --> 00:41:35.867
By destroying half the world.

483
00:41:36.035 --> 00:41:38.412
Those who survive
will happily follow a leader...

484
00:41:38.579 --> 00:41:41.415
who offers food, comfort and order.

485
00:41:41.582 --> 00:41:42.833
That could work.

486
00:41:43.001 --> 00:41:44.751
It will work.

487
00:41:44.919 --> 00:41:49.548
To you, my warlords, I offer dominion over
as much of what remains of the planet...

488
00:41:49.716 --> 00:41:53.760
as each of you can hold,
second only to me.

489
00:41:53.928 --> 00:41:55.429
Interested?

490
00:41:55.596 --> 00:41:57.723
You haven't left us much choice.

491
00:41:57.890 --> 00:42:01.268
Heh, how do you propose
to kill that many people?

492
00:42:01.436 --> 00:42:04.771
Even without the Justice League,
they will fight.

493
00:42:05.481 --> 00:42:07.733
They'll lose.

494
00:43:52.046 --> 00:43:53.964
Why are you guys
attacking Wonder Woman?

495
00:43:54.549 --> 00:43:56.091
Get out of my face, tin man.

496
00:43:56.259 --> 00:43:59.845
I've had enough trouble with superheroes
today to last me a lifetime.

497
00:44:00.012 --> 00:44:03.723
Not as much as you're gonna have
if you don't give me a straight answer.

498
00:44:03.891 --> 00:44:07.185
She was fighting the Cheetah,
then suddenly started attacking everyone.

499
00:44:07.353 --> 00:44:09.688
We got the civilians out
and the park sealed off...

500
00:44:09.856 --> 00:44:11.189
but we can't get near her.

501
00:44:11.357 --> 00:44:13.483
Look at her.
She's having a seizure or something.

502
00:44:18.489 --> 00:44:19.573
You could be right.

503
00:44:19.740 --> 00:44:22.659
Her pulse, blood pressure and respiration
are off the charts.

504
00:44:22.827 --> 00:44:25.370
If she keeps going at that pace,
she's gonna drop dead.

505
00:44:25.538 --> 00:44:27.998
That's not the worst outcome
I can imagine right now.

506
00:44:28.166 --> 00:44:31.501
I'm gonna talk her down.
Pull your men back.

507
00:44:32.253 --> 00:44:34.713
All officers,
stand down and retreat to barriers.

508
00:44:34.881 --> 00:44:36.923
Repeat, stand down.

509
00:44:46.309 --> 00:44:47.934
You must be the real one.

510
00:44:48.102 --> 00:44:51.188
Whatever that weapon is, Cheetah,
it won't work.

511
00:44:51.355 --> 00:44:54.232
It's a scanner.
Something's happening to you.

512
00:44:54.400 --> 00:44:55.901
Did you just call me Cheetah?

513
00:45:01.824 --> 00:45:03.241
She thinks I'm Cheetah.

514
00:45:22.136 --> 00:45:24.262
Wonder Woman,
just listen for a minute.

515
00:45:24.972 --> 00:45:27.599
Whatever it looks like, I'm not Cheetah.

516
00:45:27.767 --> 00:45:31.978
Think about it. All those dozens
of Cheetahs you saw, how is that possible?

517
00:45:32.146 --> 00:45:33.563
I don't know.

518
00:45:33.731 --> 00:45:34.814
I think I do.

519
00:45:35.233 --> 00:45:37.442
My sensors have detected
a cluster of nanomachines...

520
00:45:37.610 --> 00:45:38.985
attached to your brain stem.

521
00:45:40.154 --> 00:45:43.323
They're broadcasting
into your visual and auditory centers...

522
00:45:43.491 --> 00:45:45.784
making you see
whatever Cheetah wants you to.

523
00:45:46.661 --> 00:45:49.079
- It could be.
- It is.

524
00:45:49.247 --> 00:45:51.081
She knows you'll never quit a fight.

525
00:45:51.249 --> 00:45:53.667
You're supposed to keep going
until your heart gives out...

526
00:45:53.834 --> 00:45:57.462
or you have an aneurism,
or a cop gets lucky and shoots you.

527
00:45:57.630 --> 00:46:00.340
I've identified the frequency.
I'm gonna broadcast inter...

528
00:46:00.508 --> 00:46:01.675
No!

529
00:46:08.516 --> 00:46:11.434
I'm sorry you forced me to do this,
Cheetah.

530
00:46:13.854 --> 00:46:16.022
Let's get you some medical attention.

531
00:46:18.776 --> 00:46:20.527
After you.

532
00:46:33.291 --> 00:46:34.374
Cyborg?

533
00:46:34.542 --> 00:46:35.625
That's me, all right.

534
00:46:36.544 --> 00:46:40.380
You wanna tell me
what the hell is going on here?

535
00:46:45.553 --> 00:46:46.636
Where have you been?

536
00:46:46.804 --> 00:46:49.597
When I saw the grave restored,
I assumed you'd gone after...

537
00:46:49.765 --> 00:46:50.807
Later. I'm busy.

538
00:46:52.226 --> 00:46:55.145
Bruce, Superman's been shot.

539
00:46:57.315 --> 00:47:00.066
Surgeons bought to the scene
have been unable to operate.

540
00:47:00.234 --> 00:47:05.071
Superman's invulnerable flesh has thus
far resisted all attempts to cut...

541
00:47:05.239 --> 00:47:08.074
Flash, listen carefully.
Go to S.T.A.R. Labs Kyoto...

542
00:47:08.242 --> 00:47:11.494
and have them forge a piece of
kryptonite into a scalpel. Bring it...

543
00:47:11.662 --> 00:47:14.581
Can't help you. I've got a bomb
bolted to my wrist. If I stop...

544
00:47:14.749 --> 00:47:17.751
- It'll explode.
- Yeah. I'm starting to get tired.

545
00:47:17.918 --> 00:47:19.919
I'll have to try something soon.

546
00:47:20.087 --> 00:47:22.547
Keep running. I'll call back when I can.

547
00:47:22.715 --> 00:47:24.924
How did you know
what was happening to Flash?

548
00:47:25.092 --> 00:47:26.551
J'onn, I need your help. J'onn?

549
00:47:27.928 --> 00:47:30.305
J'onn? J'onn!

550
00:47:34.352 --> 00:47:35.894
It's Batman. What's happening?

551
00:47:36.062 --> 00:47:37.437
Batman!

552
00:47:37.605 --> 00:47:39.522
I'm still burning!

553
00:47:40.107 --> 00:47:42.859
Get the Batwing ready.
The Justice League is under attack.

554
00:47:43.027 --> 00:47:45.779
- By whom?
- By me.

555
00:47:56.374 --> 00:47:57.832
Batman to Justice League.

556
00:47:58.000 --> 00:47:59.042
Wonder Woman here.

557
00:47:59.210 --> 00:48:01.002
- Are you all right?
- I am now.

558
00:48:01.170 --> 00:48:02.379
I'm with Cyborg.

559
00:48:02.546 --> 00:48:05.715
Bring him. The plans don't account
for him. He could be the key.

560
00:48:05.883 --> 00:48:07.884
Key to what?
What's going on, Batman?

561
00:48:08.052 --> 00:48:09.094
Do you know something?

562
00:48:09.261 --> 00:48:11.262
The Justice League
is in extreme danger.

563
00:48:11.430 --> 00:48:14.766
You don't say. Listen, I can't keep running.
I think I can vibrate...

564
00:48:14.934 --> 00:48:17.143
No. It won't work. You have to trust me.

565
00:48:17.311 --> 00:48:18.436
You got a better idea?

566
00:48:18.604 --> 00:48:21.272
Slightly. How far away are you
from an iceberg?

567
00:48:21.440 --> 00:48:24.776
I'm never far from anything.
You think that'll slow it down enough?

568
00:48:24.944 --> 00:48:27.404
- Just. But you make one misstep...
- Got it.

569
00:48:27.571 --> 00:48:30.448
At least if it doesn't work,
nobody dies but me.

570
00:49:19.582 --> 00:49:21.374
Argh!

571
00:49:25.838 --> 00:49:28.339
Flash. Flash, are you okay?

572
00:49:32.887 --> 00:49:38.224
Not the way I would have bet
two seconds ago, but, yeah, I'm fine.

573
00:49:38.392 --> 00:49:40.143
Now, everyone, listen very carefully.

574
00:49:40.311 --> 00:49:42.604
We can still save
Superman and Green Lantern...

575
00:49:42.771 --> 00:49:45.732
if you do exactly what I say.

576
00:49:51.739 --> 00:49:52.822
How are you feeling?

577
00:49:53.324 --> 00:49:54.741
Fine.

578
00:49:54.909 --> 00:49:56.743
You injected me with aluminum oxide?

579
00:49:56.911 --> 00:49:59.078
On Batman's instruction.

580
00:49:59.246 --> 00:50:00.538
Interesting.

581
00:50:00.706 --> 00:50:02.582
It's harmless to my martian physiology...

582
00:50:02.750 --> 00:50:06.920
but ideal for neutralizing the magnesium
I was secreting.

583
00:50:07.087 --> 00:50:08.838
How did he know?

584
00:50:09.006 --> 00:50:10.590
We'll ask him when we see him.

585
00:50:10.758 --> 00:50:12.759
Right now, you have to prep for surgery.

586
00:50:25.064 --> 00:50:26.105
Hal.

587
00:50:26.649 --> 00:50:27.899
Hal, listen to me.

588
00:50:28.067 --> 00:50:31.027
However it looks, this wasn't your fault.

589
00:50:31.195 --> 00:50:33.446
Who's fault was it, then?

590
00:50:33.614 --> 00:50:37.116
I was the one with the most powerful
weapon in the universe.

591
00:50:37.284 --> 00:50:41.120
I was the one whose arrogance
led to this girl's death.

592
00:50:41.664 --> 00:50:44.207
I know more than a little
about arrogance.

593
00:50:44.375 --> 00:50:48.086
I also know about dead bodies,
and that isn't one.

594
00:50:51.298 --> 00:50:53.091
She's a sophisticated android.

595
00:50:53.259 --> 00:50:54.676
They all were.

596
00:50:54.843 --> 00:50:58.888
The entire scenario was created
to convince you that you made a bad call.

597
00:50:59.306 --> 00:51:01.140
But you didn't.

598
00:51:01.308 --> 00:51:02.934
- I was afraid that...
- No.

599
00:51:03.102 --> 00:51:05.395
You weren't afraid. Not really.

600
00:51:05.563 --> 00:51:09.232
You were dosed with a synthesized version
of the Scarecrow's fear gas...

601
00:51:09.400 --> 00:51:11.901
because will
is the source of your strength.

602
00:51:12.069 --> 00:51:15.488
And fear is the enemy of will.

603
00:51:15.656 --> 00:51:17.574
I've got the antidote to the fear gas.

604
00:51:17.741 --> 00:51:19.617
Don't need it.

605
00:51:28.335 --> 00:51:31.504
Robots, advanced drugs,
psychological profiling.

606
00:51:31.672 --> 00:51:34.007
No way Star Sapphire
came up with this on her own.

607
00:51:34.174 --> 00:51:35.592
I did this to you.

608
00:51:36.343 --> 00:51:38.303
To all of you.

609
00:51:41.765 --> 00:51:44.183
You want me to perform surgery
on him?

610
00:51:44.351 --> 00:51:45.643
You're the only one who can.

611
00:51:45.811 --> 00:51:47.520
Flash is at S.T.A.R. Labs Kyoto...

612
00:51:47.688 --> 00:51:49.981
waiting for them to finish
making a kryptonite scalpel.

613
00:51:50.149 --> 00:51:51.691
Nothing else can cut his skin.

614
00:51:51.859 --> 00:51:53.151
But we've run out of time.

615
00:51:53.319 --> 00:51:56.029
Your shapeshifting powers
are his best hope.

616
00:51:56.196 --> 00:51:57.322
This can work.

617
00:51:57.489 --> 00:51:59.574
I'm glad you think so.

618
00:52:00.034 --> 00:52:01.784
You're going to be doing
the cutting.

619
00:52:01.952 --> 00:52:04.120
Who with the what now?

620
00:52:05.080 --> 00:52:06.122
What's that?

621
00:52:06.290 --> 00:52:09.292
A piece of kryptonite
that you're going to use like a lens.

622
00:52:09.460 --> 00:52:13.046
Narrow your blaster to minimum
and filter it through.

623
00:52:13.547 --> 00:52:15.882
I really don't know if I can...

624
00:52:16.717 --> 00:52:18.384
Please.

625
00:52:20.304 --> 00:52:21.888
Tell me what to do.

626
00:52:26.560 --> 00:52:28.353
That's good.

627
00:52:28.520 --> 00:52:30.396
We're ready for you now.

628
00:52:40.991 --> 00:52:42.575
I have it.

629
00:53:15.484 --> 00:53:16.734
All right!

630
00:53:16.902 --> 00:53:18.695
Yeah!

631
00:53:18.862 --> 00:53:20.571
What happened?

632
00:53:21.031 --> 00:53:23.241
Why don't you ask him?

633
00:53:30.082 --> 00:53:32.333
It was a coordinated attack
intended to kill us...

634
00:53:32.501 --> 00:53:35.795
or, failing that, put us out of
commission for an extended period.

635
00:53:35.963 --> 00:53:39.465
Obviously the first step of a larger
scheme, something that we would stop.

636
00:53:39.633 --> 00:53:41.801
The attacks were strategically brilliant.

637
00:53:41.969 --> 00:53:46.305
They were specifically targeted at our
physical and psychological weaknesses.

638
00:53:46.473 --> 00:53:49.600
Obviously by someone
who knows us very well.

639
00:53:49.768 --> 00:53:51.102
The plans were mine.

640
00:53:51.270 --> 00:53:53.146
- Yours?
- Say what, now?

641
00:53:53.313 --> 00:53:56.774
I've carefully studied
every Justice Leaguer, past and present...

642
00:53:56.942 --> 00:53:59.152
and created contingency plans
to neutralize you...

643
00:53:59.319 --> 00:54:02.238
- ...should that become necessary.
- You've gotta be kidding me.

644
00:54:02.406 --> 00:54:04.449
Neutralize, not kill.

645
00:54:04.616 --> 00:54:07.160
Whoever implemented my plans
altered them.

646
00:54:07.327 --> 00:54:10.288
It's still a completely unacceptable
breach of our trust.

647
00:54:10.456 --> 00:54:12.915
The Justice League
are among the most powerful...

648
00:54:13.083 --> 00:54:15.084
and potentially dangerous people
on the planet.

649
00:54:15.252 --> 00:54:17.587
You think one of us
would go over to the other side?

650
00:54:17.755 --> 00:54:20.840
Or succumb to mind control.
Yes, it's possible.

651
00:54:21.008 --> 00:54:24.010
That's why I developed plans
for containing any or all members...

652
00:54:24.178 --> 00:54:26.637
of the JLA should the need ever arise.

653
00:54:26.805 --> 00:54:28.806
None of us would ever do that to you.

654
00:54:28.974 --> 00:54:30.850
Then you're damned fools.

655
00:54:32.478 --> 00:54:34.270
Where do you think you're going?

656
00:54:36.732 --> 00:54:39.025
I'm just a visitor.
This is getting personal.

657
00:54:39.193 --> 00:54:41.319
Stay. You're part of this now.

658
00:54:44.656 --> 00:54:47.617
I'm not sure I have a problem
with Batman's contingency plans.

659
00:54:47.785 --> 00:54:50.328
But letting somebody steal them
was pretty damned dumb.

660
00:54:50.496 --> 00:54:53.956
I've had some time to think about that
and I know how it happened.

661
00:54:55.584 --> 00:54:58.002
Security video from the Batcave.

662
00:54:58.170 --> 00:55:00.463
He's in hologram form...

663
00:55:01.048 --> 00:55:04.383
so the motion detectors
didn't have anything to lock on to.

664
00:55:06.637 --> 00:55:10.181
Mirror Master's not that careful.
And the technology, the scope of all this?

665
00:55:10.349 --> 00:55:11.474
He's not working alone.

666
00:55:11.642 --> 00:55:14.310
The video's from the night
we caught the Royal Flush Gang.

667
00:55:14.478 --> 00:55:17.188
Whoever set them up
with that interdimensional lock pick...

668
00:55:17.356 --> 00:55:21.067
also gave Mirror Master the means
to steal encrypted files.

669
00:55:21.235 --> 00:55:23.945
But the encryption
on your files is all but unbreakable.

670
00:55:24.112 --> 00:55:25.321
All but.

671
00:55:25.489 --> 00:55:26.531
I can find them.

672
00:55:26.698 --> 00:55:30.576
As you say, my encryption is formidable, but
in the event that it ever was cracked...

673
00:55:30.744 --> 00:55:32.703
You had a contingency plan.

674
00:55:32.871 --> 00:55:35.248
When my files are decrypted,
they call home.

675
00:55:38.502 --> 00:55:39.836
Louisiana.

676
00:55:40.003 --> 00:55:41.921
Swampland.

677
00:55:46.093 --> 00:55:49.720
So that thing's really going
to kill half the population of Earth.

678
00:55:49.888 --> 00:55:50.930
Not exactly.

679
00:55:51.098 --> 00:55:53.099
The solar flare
will do most of the damage.

680
00:55:53.267 --> 00:55:54.851
Solar flare?

681
00:55:55.018 --> 00:55:56.769
Think of this as a pilot light.

682
00:55:56.937 --> 00:55:59.856
When our ideal launch window opens
in just over an hour...

683
00:56:00.023 --> 00:56:02.650
this magnificent creation
will fly into the sun...

684
00:56:02.818 --> 00:56:04.569
trailing magnetic resonance.

685
00:56:04.736 --> 00:56:07.238
- And when it hits?
- It will trigger a solar flare...

686
00:56:07.406 --> 00:56:11.576
that will propagate at light speed
along the magnetic trail we've left.

687
00:56:11.743 --> 00:56:13.286
Eight and a half minutes later...

688
00:56:13.453 --> 00:56:16.539
it will utterly destroy
the sunward-facing side of the Earth.

689
00:56:16.707 --> 00:56:19.792
Nearly half the world's population
will die instantly.

690
00:56:19.960 --> 00:56:22.670
And thanks to the accompanying
electromagnetic pulse...

691
00:56:22.838 --> 00:56:26.632
any technology more advanced
than, say, the steam engine...

692
00:56:26.800 --> 00:56:28.467
will simply stop working.

693
00:56:28.635 --> 00:56:33.306
No technology, no superheroes,
no functioning governments.

694
00:56:33.473 --> 00:56:35.224
Except the one we control.

695
00:56:35.392 --> 00:56:37.435
That's quite an ambitious plan.

696
00:56:39.646 --> 00:56:41.480
No wonder you wanted us
out of the way.

697
00:56:41.648 --> 00:56:44.942
- I thought you took care of him.
- He should've been burning for weeks.

698
00:56:45.110 --> 00:56:46.277
Don't feel bad.

699
00:56:46.445 --> 00:56:49.071
Actually, none of you managed
to finish the job.

700
00:56:49.239 --> 00:56:51.157
Did you get all that?

701
00:56:52.117 --> 00:56:53.618
We did.

702
00:56:56.496 --> 00:56:58.497
Take them down.

703
00:56:58.999 --> 00:57:01.167
Don't let them get to the missile.

704
00:57:37.663 --> 00:57:38.704
Ha!

705
00:57:48.006 --> 00:57:50.466
I still can't believe
what you tried to do to me.

706
00:57:50.634 --> 00:57:51.884
You hurt me, Jordan.

707
00:57:52.052 --> 00:57:55.221
You broke my heart, and I'll never
stop trying to hurt you back.

708
00:58:11.405 --> 00:58:12.905
That's new.

709
00:58:21.081 --> 00:58:24.000
You didn't think it'd be that easy,
did you?

710
00:59:17.804 --> 00:59:19.722
Didn't I bury you alive?

711
00:59:19.890 --> 00:59:21.891
That's where you made your mistake.

712
00:59:22.059 --> 00:59:24.477
I won't repeat it.

713
01:00:13.026 --> 01:00:17.530
You're good, but lately,
I've had a lot of practice fighting you.

714
01:00:44.391 --> 01:00:46.392
Where's the flipping
countdown command?

715
01:00:53.150 --> 01:00:55.568
Missile launch aborted.

716
01:01:37.903 --> 01:01:40.404
You never asked me
how my wrist was healing.

717
01:01:40.947 --> 01:01:43.949
Fine, how's your...? Unh!

718
01:01:44.701 --> 01:01:46.785
Surprisingly fast.

719
01:01:57.255 --> 01:02:00.257
Manual launch sequence engaged.

720
01:02:34.709 --> 01:02:35.709
Ah!

721
01:03:15.292 --> 01:03:18.877
Welcome to the dawn of a new world.

722
01:03:34.936 --> 01:03:36.645
I've got work to do.

723
01:04:33.536 --> 01:04:36.080
I do keep hurting you, don't I?

724
01:04:37.374 --> 01:04:38.624
Savage launched the weapon.

725
01:04:38.792 --> 01:04:41.460
- Superman's already in pursuit.
- On it.

726
01:04:47.300 --> 01:04:49.009
Superman, where are you?

727
01:04:49.177 --> 01:04:50.427
I'm approaching the missile.

728
01:04:50.845 --> 01:04:54.306
I should easily be able to intercept it
before it detonates.

729
01:05:23.711 --> 01:05:26.547
- Superman?
- Can't talk now.

730
01:05:46.651 --> 01:05:48.193
No.

731
01:06:16.347 --> 01:06:17.806
The solar flare is coming.

732
01:06:17.974 --> 01:06:19.099
How do we stop it?

733
01:06:19.267 --> 01:06:23.228
I don't know, but we've got less than
eight minutes to figure something out.

734
01:06:25.565 --> 01:06:27.232
Maybe longer.

735
01:06:49.881 --> 01:06:51.840
- Not much blood.
- Not much back.

736
01:06:54.344 --> 01:06:57.012
- You think he'll stop it?
- He'll stop it.

737
01:06:57.180 --> 01:07:01.266
Not this time. Flare's on its way. We've got
seven minutes to come up with something.

738
01:07:01.434 --> 01:07:02.434
Seven minutes?

739
01:07:02.602 --> 01:07:05.604
Hal's gonna try to buy us more,
but that's all we can count on.

740
01:07:29.921 --> 01:07:31.964
Maybe I could move
the Earth out of the way?

741
01:07:32.131 --> 01:07:34.383
If we had a week, I couldn't list
all the reasons that won't work.

742
01:07:34.551 --> 01:07:36.885
- You have a plan?
- No, but Savage does.

743
01:07:37.303 --> 01:07:40.472
This place is going to be sun side
by the time the flare gets here.

744
01:07:40.640 --> 01:07:42.182
The Legion wasn't worried either.

745
01:07:42.350 --> 01:07:45.561
There must be some mechanism
to protect them from the flare.

746
01:07:46.646 --> 01:07:49.439
Start talking.
I don't have time for niceties.

747
01:07:49.607 --> 01:07:52.276
You don't have time
to break an immortal either.

748
01:07:52.443 --> 01:07:53.819
Don't have to.

749
01:07:53.987 --> 01:07:56.154
I know how they intended to survive.

750
01:07:56.322 --> 01:07:58.991
The intangibility tech
he gave the Royal Flush Gang.

751
01:07:59.158 --> 01:08:00.576
It must've been a test run.

752
01:08:00.743 --> 01:08:03.412
Sure, just let the flare
pass right through this place.

753
01:08:03.580 --> 01:08:06.081
But where's the apparatus?
It would have to be huge.

754
01:08:06.249 --> 01:08:09.585
That's the beauty part.
The Hall of Doom is the apparatus.

755
01:08:09.752 --> 01:08:13.088
I already downloaded the specs
when I interfaced with the control panel.

756
01:08:13.256 --> 01:08:17.342
Can this building generate a signal strong
enough to make the whole Earth intangible?

757
01:08:17.510 --> 01:08:18.927
If we had enough power.

758
01:08:19.095 --> 01:08:21.096
Also, it would help if it were higher up.

759
01:08:21.264 --> 01:08:23.015
- How high?
- Low orbit.

760
01:08:23.182 --> 01:08:24.808
I can help you out with that.

761
01:08:31.024 --> 01:08:33.859
Everybody knows their jobs. Go.

762
01:09:42.011 --> 01:09:43.053
Ah!

763
01:09:49.102 --> 01:09:50.477
J'onn?

764
01:09:50.645 --> 01:09:53.230
It's Green Lantern.
His shield just failed.

765
01:09:53.398 --> 01:09:55.941
The solar flare is on its way.

766
01:09:57.443 --> 01:09:59.861
What about it?
Is the displacement field ready?

767
01:10:00.029 --> 01:10:02.614
- I think so, I'd like to test...
- This is the test.

768
01:11:33.748 --> 01:11:35.874
I'm calling this official meeting to order.

769
01:11:36.042 --> 01:11:38.543
First, some news
for those of you who haven't heard.

770
01:11:38.711 --> 01:11:41.213
The world court
has just found Vandal Savage guilty...

771
01:11:41.380 --> 01:11:42.881
of crimes against humanity.

772
01:11:43.049 --> 01:11:44.549
Tell them what the immortal got.

773
01:11:44.717 --> 01:11:48.470
Life in prison,
without possibility of parole.

774
01:11:50.181 --> 01:11:52.724
A little new business.
I want to officially welcome...

775
01:11:52.892 --> 01:11:57.562
the newest member of the Justice League
by unanimous consent, Cyborg.

776
01:11:57.730 --> 01:11:58.980
Nice. Way to go.

777
01:11:59.148 --> 01:12:00.899
- Good job.
- Congratulations, Victor.

778
01:12:01.275 --> 01:12:02.734
Thanks, everybody.

779
01:12:02.902 --> 01:12:05.278
And now, the main reason
I called this session.

780
01:12:05.446 --> 01:12:09.533
In light of the breach of trust revealed
to us during the Vandal Savage matter...

781
01:12:09.700 --> 01:12:13.745
we have to decide whether Batman
should be allowed to remain in the league.

782
01:12:14.163 --> 01:12:16.373
- All those in favor of...
- Wait.

783
01:12:16.541 --> 01:12:19.918
Before we vote, the accused should be
allowed a few words in his defense.

784
01:12:20.086 --> 01:12:21.169
Seconded.

785
01:12:21.587 --> 01:12:23.588
Okay. Batman?

786
01:12:23.756 --> 01:12:25.924
My actions don't require any defense.

787
01:12:26.092 --> 01:12:28.385
In the same situation, I'd do it again.

788
01:12:28.553 --> 01:12:29.678
Oh, come on.

789
01:12:29.846 --> 01:12:32.472
As individuals,
and even more so as a group...

790
01:12:32.640 --> 01:12:35.433
the Justice League is too dangerous
to lack a fail-safe...

791
01:12:35.601 --> 01:12:37.602
against any possible misuse
of our power.

792
01:12:37.770 --> 01:12:41.064
We use our power to protect the world.
We always have.

793
01:12:41.232 --> 01:12:44.484
And what if we ever used it
for some other purpose?

794
01:12:44.652 --> 01:12:48.947
If you people can't see the potential danger
of an out-of-control Justice League...

795
01:12:49.115 --> 01:12:51.449
I don't need to wait for a vote.

796
01:12:52.118 --> 01:12:54.160
I don't belong here.

797
01:13:16.100 --> 01:13:17.559
Got a minute?

798
01:13:20.771 --> 01:13:21.813
What do you want?

799
01:13:21.981 --> 01:13:24.858
You made contingency plans
to stop everybody in the League...

800
01:13:25.026 --> 01:13:26.985
just in case any of us ever went bad.

801
01:13:27.403 --> 01:13:30.405
My contingencies
were intended to immobilize, not kill.

802
01:13:30.573 --> 01:13:33.241
But Savage came up with the plan
to bury you.

803
01:13:33.409 --> 01:13:35.994
I assume so. It wasn't one of mine.

804
01:13:36.996 --> 01:13:38.163
Was that it?

805
01:13:38.331 --> 01:13:40.832
With all that talk
about unchecked power...

806
01:13:41.000 --> 01:13:45.003
you're still so arrogant you didn't bother
to come up with a plan to stop yourself?

807
01:13:45.922 --> 01:13:47.672
I do have a plan.

808
01:13:47.840 --> 01:13:49.841
It's called the Justice League.

809
01:13:51.344 --> 01:13:53.470
Just wanted to be sure.

810
01:13:56.641 --> 01:13:57.682
What is it?

811
01:13:57.850 --> 01:14:00.226
If the league ever did go over
to the wrong side...

812
01:14:00.394 --> 01:14:03.688
I want there to be somebody I can trust
to keep the planet safe.

813
01:14:04.357 --> 01:14:06.232
Even from me.
